  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A family beach of about 350 metres between Cap Camarat and Cap Taillat (Ramatuelle tourist office), with fine sand and crystal-clear water. L'Escalet has a handy extra for four-legged visitors: two rinse showers side by side near the car park — not a dedicated dog shower, but ordinary showers under which you can very well rinse your dog after a swim.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>As on the other Ramatuelle beaches, dogs on a leash are accepted according to the tourist office (FAQ consulted 29 October 2026) — the leash is confirmed on site by a Ramatuelle town sign ("Tenez votre chien en laisse"). The Domaine de l'Escalet site (beach access) is open from 6am to 10pm, 7 days a week, according to the town hall's signage. Two ordinary rinse showers (not a dedicated dog shower) are available side by side near the car park — also handy for rinsing sand and salt from your dog's coat after a swim. Fires are banned on the site (municipal bylaw), and motorhomes are not allowed to park on the Domaine's private road.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: arrive early in the morning, before the car park fills up — late morning is the busiest time in summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/fiche-balade-cap-camarat-ramatuelle">coastal path links L'Escalet to Cap Camarat and its lighthouse</a>, a nice walk to extend the day on foot with your dog after a swim.</p>
